            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0236" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23574: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-12T23:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1920—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 13—5:12
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>101. In secret visit tonight to Embassy General Benjamin Hill declared that
                    Sonora is now openly rebellious; Federal soldiers now there, as well as rebel
                    groups including Villa and the majority of Federals throughout Mexico, will aid
                    Obregón in the revolt; General Diéguez, at present at Guadalajara, is afraid to
                    go to Sonora to his troops; there is no expectation of a [garbled group],
                    although preparations are complete for an overturn of the Government which <pb
                        facs="0237" n="137" xml:id="pg137"/> will conclude the Obregón–Carranza
                    dispute; and the rebel troops will probably be commanded by Hill and Obregón who
                    will try from Mexico City to join the troops already organized for them not far
                    off.</p>
                <p>In event of his failure to leave Mexico City, Hill asks asylum here in Embassy
                    for self and family. He is informed Department will be asked to advise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
